# spec_id: eravos.organism.breath · version 2.0.0 · phase P8.4 → P44 (rebuilt: "same with breath") · status canonical
# source: v10 VAGAL_INSTRUMENT (polyvagal breath instrument, VAGAL mode)
identity:
  id: eravos.breath ; label: Breath ; icon: ◎ ; accent: "#8844ff"
  comp_intent: A paced-breathing guide that is also an instrument — the music swells on the inhale and falls on the exhale, so you can breathe with it, for one breath or a timed session.
  novelty: Only organism whose clock is a breath cycle (seconds per segment) rather than bars; emits continuous breath control signals.
engine:
  cycle: a list of segments [phase, seconds, level] — in · sip (top-up inhale) · hold · out · rest — so double-inhale patterns are exact
  patterns: COHERENCE 5·5 · RESONANCE 5.5·5.5 · 4-7-8 · BOX 4·4·4·4 · TRIANGLE 4·4·4 · EXTENDED 4·8 · 2-TO-1 3·6 · PHYSIOLOGICAL SIGH (2.2 to 0.8, 0.8 sip to 1, 6 out, 1 rest)
            · UJJAYI 6·6 · SLEEP 4·8·rest 3 · ENERGIZE 2·2 · HANGING TREE 6·2·6·2 · CUSTOM in/hold/out/rest (0.5–30 s)
  shape: pace ×0.5–2 ; curve sine · linear · natural (quick then settling) · late (slow then quick) ; tempo link: cycle snapped to whole bars
  session: open | 1 · 3 · 5 · 10 · 15 · 20 min — ends at a cycle boundary with three bells, pauses, emits breath:session {state:'done', seconds, cycles}, logs it (date, minutes, cycles, pattern; last 60 kept with the window)
           programs: steady · slow down (cycle × 1 → 1.4 over the session) · longer exhale (exhale × 1 → 1.6)
  outputs: port 'breath' = floor + depth·(1 − floor)·breath ; 'inverse' = 1 − breath ; 'gate' = 1 during in/sip ; breath:phase {phase, cycle, time, duration} per inhale / hold / exhale / rest (not per sip)
  voice: pad (3 detuned triangles) · choir (3 saws through /a/ formants 730 + 1090 Hz) · drone (saw + fifth) · air only ; chord fifth/minor/major/sus2/octaves/minor 9 ; octave 1–6 ;
         rise ±12 st on the inhale ; brightness ; AIR (looping noise, band-pass that opens and swells with the breath) ; bells bell · bowl · chime · click on in/out turns ; level
  guide: optional spoken "in · hold · out · rest" (speechSynthesis, from the UI, on the audio clock)
hooks: breath.hook.breath_out · inverse_out · gate_out (out ; modulation) ; phase_out (breath:phase) ; session_out (breath:session) ; STD.audio_out ; STD.theory_in
ui: orb (the real signal) inside a ring of the cycle's segments with a needle at now ; phase word + countdown ; cycle, breaths/min, time left / in ; a 60-second trace ;
    pattern · session · program · voice guide · snap to bars ; custom lengths only for CUSTOM ; pace, curve ; sound ; depth, floor ; sessions log (this week)
safety note in UI: "Stop if you feel dizzy." (4-7-8 and ENERGIZE) — plain text, no medical claims
tests: BOX → phases each 4.0 s ± 10 ms ; breath = 1 at end of inhale, 0 at end of exhale ; tempoLink → whole bars ; physiological sigh levels 0.8 → 1 → 0 ;
       outputs floor/depth, inverse, gate exact ; 1-minute session ends after 6 cycles with a log entry ; longer exhale grows only the exhale ; every voice and preset audible

